## 🔄 **Development Workflow**

### Phase 1: Project Initialization
```bash
# 1. Parse project requirements
task-master parse-prd --input="requirements.md" --research

# 2. Analyze complexity and feasibility
task-master analyze-complexity --research

# 3. Generate initial task breakdown
task-master expand --all --research

# 4. Create development milestones
task-master generate-milestones --research
```

### Phase 2: Sprint Planning
```bash
# 1. Select tasks for current sprint
task-master select-tasks --sprint=1 --capacity=40h

# 2. Research selected tasks
task-master research-tasks --sprint=1

# 3. Refine task estimates
task-master refine-estimates --sprint=1 --research

# 4. Generate sprint documentation
task-master generate-sprint-docs --sprint=1
```

### Phase 3: Development Execution
```bash
# 1. Start task with research context
task-master start --id="T001" --research

# 2. Get task-specific guidance
task-master guide --id="T001" --step="implementation"

# 3. Research on-demand
task-master research "specific technical challenge" --task="T001"

# 4. Update task progress
task-master update --id="T001" --status="in-progress" --notes="Implementation details"
```

### Phase 4: Review & Integration
```bash
# 1. Review completed tasks
task-master review --completed --research

# 2. Generate integration tasks
task-master generate-integration-tasks --research

# 3. Update project documentation
task-master update-docs --auto

# 4. Prepare next sprint
task-master prepare-next-sprint --research
```

